   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1: Increased active participation of women in communities in community action to mitigate climate-induced conflict risks
Outcome Indicator 1a: Proportion of women in target communities participating in/contributing to peacebuilding within communities by age.
Output 1.1: Capacity of women community leadership particularly in climate-induced conflicts and in the development of climate adaptation measures is strengthened.
Activity 1.1.1 Delivering training of women community leaders in awareness of climate-induced risks and local approaches/ to mitigate risks (UNDP)
Output Indicator 1.1.1:  Women&#x2019;s self-rating of their understanding of climate-related security risks.
Activity 1.1.2 Support community-led establishment of inclusive community civic spaces to facilitate collective decision-making (UNDP)
Output Indicator 1.1.2: Women&#x2019;s self-rating of their ability to contribute toward adaptation needs.
Output Indicator 1.1.3: 
Proportion of community members in target communities who believe that community dialogue is inclusive for women participation and responsive to undertaken climate and conflict-sensitive actions, by sex and age. 

Outcome 2:  Communities and households have improved resilience to manage risks and mitigate shocks from conflict and human induced/natural disasters
Outcome Indicator 2a: Assessed vulnerability of target communities.
Output 2.2: Provincial policies and strategic frameworks are informed by climate-induced peace and security risks.
Activity 2.2.1 Conduct of provincial and sub-provincial climate risk assessment in both Hela and Southern Highlands provinces (UNDP)
Output Indicator 2.2.1: Number of communities targeted for support in development and implementation of community peace for development plans informed through provincial and sub-provincial climate risk assessments.
Activity 2.2.2 Support provincial authorities in development of provincial climate and gender-sensitive peace and security strategies with costed provincial action</narrative>
    </description>
